Let G be a torsionfree group Then:
1. Kn(ZG) = 0 for n ≤ −1;
2. The reduced projective class group K̃0(ZG) vanishes;
3. The Whitehead group Wh(G) vanishes;
4. For any homomorphism w: G → {±1} the w-twisted L-theoretic assembly map
Hn(BG; wL⟨−∞⟩) ∼=→ L⟨−∞⟩n(RG,w) is bijective.

If M is an aspherical closed manifold of even dimension, then
(−1)dim(M)/2 · χ(M) ≥ 0.

If M is a closed Riemannian manifold of even dimension with sectional curvature sec(M), then
(−1)dim(M)/2 · χ(M) > 0 if sec(M) < 0;
(−1)dim(M)/2 · χ(M) ≥ 0 if sec(M) ≤ 0;
χ(M) ≥ 0 if sec(M) ≥ 0;
χ(M) > 0 if sec(M) > 0.

Let M be an aspherical closed orientable manifold. Suppose that its simplicial volume ||M|| vanishes. Then M̃ is of determinant class and
b(2)p(M̃) = 0 for p ≥ 0;
ρ(2)(M̃) = 0.
